# --------------------- gwf sgd options ---------------------
# flopy multi-package
# package-type stress-package

block options
name auxiliary
type string
shape (naux)
reader urword
optional true
longname keyword to specify aux variables
description REPLACE auxnames {'{#1}': 'Groundwater Flow'}

block options
name boundnames
type keyword
shape
reader urword
optional true
longname
description REPLACE boundnames {'{#1}': 'specified gradient boundary'}

block options
name print_input
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname print input to listing file
description REPLACE print_input {'{#1}': 'specified gradient boundary'}
mf6internal iprpak

block options
name print_flows
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname print boundary flow to listing file
description REPLACE print_flows {'{#1}': 'specified gradient boundary'}
mf6internal iprflow

block options
name save_flows
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname save boundary flows to budget file
description REPLACE save_flows {'{#1}': 'specified gradient boundary'}
mf6internal ipakcb


# --------------------- gwf sgd dimensions ---------------------

block dimensions
name maxbound
type integer
reader urword
optional false
longname maximum number of specified gradient cells
description REPLACE maxbound {'{#1}': 'specified gradient boundary'}


# --------------------- gwf sgd period ---------------------

block period
name iper
type integer
block_variable True
in_record true
tagged false
shape
valid
reader urword
optional false
longname stress period number
description REPLACE iper {}

block period
name stress_period_data
type recarray cellid gradx grady gradz hwva aux boundname
shape (maxbound)
reader urword
longname
description
mf6internal spd

block period
name cellid
type integer
shape (ncelldim)
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
longname cell identifier
description REPLACE cellid {}

block period
name gradx
type double precision
shape
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
longname specified gradient x component
description is the x component of the specified hydraulic gradient at the boundary.  The gradient points in the direction of flow (equal to the negative of the hydraulic head gradient).  For a free-drainage (unit vertical gradient) boundary GRADX is 0.0, GRADY is 0.0, and GRADZ is -1.0.

block period
name grady
type double precision
shape
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
longname specified gradient y component
description is the y component of the specified hydraulic gradient at the boundary.  The gradient points in the direction of flow (equal to the negative of the hydraulic head gradient).

block period
name gradz
type double precision
shape
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
longname specified gradient z component
description is the z component of the specified hydraulic gradient at the boundary.  The gradient points in the direction of flow (equal to the negative of the hydraulic head gradient).  A value of -1.0 (with GRADX and GRADY equal to 0.0) imposes a downward unit gradient, i.e. free drainage.

block period
name hwva
type double precision
shape
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
longname boundary face area
description is the area of the boundary face across which the specified gradient flux is applied.

block period
name aux
type double precision
in_record true
tagged false
shape (naux)
reader urword
optional true
longname auxiliary variables
description REPLACE aux {'{#1}': 'specified gradient boundary'}
mf6internal auxvar

block period
name boundname
type string
shape
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
optional true
longname specified gradient boundary name
description REPLACE boundname {'{#1}': 'specified gradient'}
